# The days line below carries no {time}, and hu-HU is the only locale of 18
# here that does not pair them, so 'ebressz fel minden hetfon 7-kor' binds
# the time text into {days}. The line added below puts the time first, where
# 'minden' separates the two slots: OVOS-INTENT-2 forbids adjacent slots, and
# Hungarian marks time with the -kor suffix rather than a preposition, so the
# shape every other locale uses has no separator word to borrow here.
# Every word below is already in this file. Both lines are kept, so the
# days-only phrasing still matches. Unvouched: hu-HU has no reviewer of
# record. Open for a speaker: whether the days-then-time order is wanted,
# which needs a literal word between the two slots that only a speaker can give.
ébressz fel [minket] [{time}(-kor|kor)]
ébressz fel {time}(-kor|kor), hogy {mediakind} szóljon
ébressz fel minden {days}
ébressz fel {time}(-kor|kor) minden {days}
